    "She looked toward the sky." 
    "The day was getting late." 
    "The blue had faded into a softer color." 
    "She should probably keep walking. Her parents would worry if she came home too slowly." 
    "Stella took another step. Then another." 
    "Her eyes were still wet. But she told herself it was only because the wind was bothering them." 
